      "weight": 0.2,
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "claim": "A bulb is a resistive load that allows current to pass while converting electrical energy to light and heat.",
      "evidence": "Bulbs obey Ohm’s law (V = IR) and have finite resistance, so current flows through them when the circuit is closed.",
